The  rmdir  utility removes the directory entry specified by each
argument, provided it is empty.  Arguments are processed  in  the
order  given.   In  order to remove both a parent directory and a
subdirectory of that parent, the subdirectory must  be  specified
first  so  the parent directory is empty when tries to remove it.
The following option is available: Each argument is treated as  a
pathname  of  which  all  components will be removed, if they are
empty, starting with the last most  component.   (See  for  fully
non‐discriminant  recursive removal.)  The utility exits with one
of the following values: Each directory entry specified by a  dir
operand  referred  to an empty directory and was removed success‐
fully.  An error occurred.  The utility is expected to be compat‐
